# strix-mimo-native-mxfp4.patch
#
# MiMo-V2 native-checkpoint conversion fix for the pinned strix converter
# (upstreams/strix-llama.cpp; conversion/mimo.py is byte-identical at the
# upstreams/llama.cpp pin). Apply with:
#
#   git -C upstreams/strix-llama.cpp apply "$PWD/patches/strix-mimo-native-mxfp4.patch"
#
# Two defects in conversion/mimo.py:
#
#   1) routed-expert scale siblings (`...weight_scale`) counted towards the
#      `n_experts * 3` merge threshold, so the merge fired while payloads were
#      still missing (KeyError: model.layers.N.mlp.experts.E.gate_proj.weight
#      near line 211). Payloads now pair with their scale siblings and only
#      complete pairs count.
#
#   2) packed native MXFP4 experts (compressed-tensors "mxfp4-pack-quantized":
#      uint8 code payload + uint8 E8M0 scale sibling) were streamed as if they
#      were dense weights. They are now repacked losslessly through the
#      existing base.repack_mxfp4_blocks into ggml block_mxfp4, written as
#      GGML_TYPE_MXFP4 expert tensors (same pattern as
#      conversion/deepseek.py::_write_mxfp4_expert_tensor), and the output
#      file type is MOSTLY_MXFP4_MOE.
#
# Second-generation candidate experts (quantization_config.store_dtype ==
# "second_gen_affine", e.g. q3_affine_g128 codes + I8 scale/zero pairs) have
# no GGML decoder: they are refused with an explicit "unsupported expert
# format: ... second_gen_affine" diagnostic instead of being mislabelled
# native MXFP4 or requantized. Dense (BF16/F16/F32) experts and the source
# TP-aware FP8 qkv conversion path are unchanged.
#
# Regression: tests/test_mimo_native_mxfp4.py (applies this patch to a
# throwaway tree copy; the pinned checkout stays immutable).
diff --git a/conversion/mimo.py b/conversion/mimo.py
index 15dbeb7..1ef2a32 100644
